{:edb/db-before-t 1397 :edb/db-after-t 1398 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534710 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:46:48.359Z" 13194139534710 true] [17592186105519 1100 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle$, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle$." 13194139534710 false] [17592186105519 1100 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" 13194139534710 true] [17592186105519 1145 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$" 13194139534710 true] [17592186105519 1145 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}1 & - 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & - 2 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = 1 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert - ( - 4 ) \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right\\vert + 2 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}0 & - 2 \\\\ - 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = ( - 2 \\cdot  3 - 1 \\cdot  0 ) + 4 ( 0 \\cdot  3 - 1 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) + 2 ( 0 \\cdot  0 - ( - 1 ) \\cdot  ( - 2 ) ) \\\\  & = - 6 + 4 - 4 \\\\  & = - 6\\end{array}$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = \\mid -6 \\mid = 6\n$$" 13194139534710 false] [17592186105520 1100 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle$, $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle$, and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." 13194139534710 false] [17592186105520 1100 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." 13194139534710 true] [17592186105520 1145 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$." 13194139534710 true] [17592186105520 1145 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ - 2 & - 1 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = k \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert - 2 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 2 & 1 \\\\ - 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right\\vert + 1 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 2 & - 1 \\\\ - 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = k ( - 1 \\cdot  2 - 1 \\cdot  1 ) - 2 ( - 2 \\cdot  2 - ( - 1 ) \\cdot  1 ) + ( - 2 \\cdot  1 - ( - 1 ) \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) \\\\  & = - 3 k + 6 - 3 \\\\  & = - 3 k + 3.\\end{array}$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  ( \\mathbf{b} \\times  \\mathbf{c} ) & = 0 \\\\ - 3 k + 3 & = 0 \\\\ k & = 1\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$." 13194139534710 false] [17592186105521 1100 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$, $\\overrightarrow{AC}$, and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$, given the points $A(3,-1,2)$, $B(2,1,1)$, $C(-1,2,1)$, and $D(4,4,2)$." 13194139534710 false] [17592186105521 1100 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" 13194139534710 true] [17592186105521 1145 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$, $\\overrightarrow{AC}$, and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\overrightarrow{AB} & = \\mathbf{b} - \\mathbf{a} \\\\  & = ( 2 \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k} ) - ( 3 \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j} + 2 \\mathbf{k} ) \\\\  & = - \\mathbf{i} + 2 \\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 1 , 2 , - 1 \\rangle \\\\ \\overrightarrow{AC} & = \\mathbf{c} - \\mathbf{a} \\\\  & = ( - \\mathbf{i} + 2 \\mathbf{j} + \\mathbf{k} ) - ( 3 \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j} + 2 \\mathbf{k} ) \\\\  & = - 4 \\mathbf{i} + 3 \\mathbf{j} - \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = \\langle  - 4 , 3 , - 1 \\rangle \\\\ \\overrightarrow{AD} & = \\mathbf{d} - \\mathbf{a} \\\\  & = ( 4 \\mathbf{i} + 4 \\mathbf{j} + 2 \\mathbf{k} ) - ( 3 \\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j} + 2 \\mathbf{k} ) \\\\  & = \\mathbf{i} + 5 \\mathbf{j} \\\\  & = \\langle  1 , 5 , 0 \\rangle\\end{array}$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\overrightarrow{AB} \\cdot  ( \\overrightarrow{AC} \\times  \\overrightarrow{AD} ) & = \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{ccc}- 1 & 2 & - 1 \\\\ - 4 & 3 & - 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = ( - 1 ) \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}3 & - 1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right\\vert - 2 \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 4 & - 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right\\vert + ( - 1 ) \\cdot  \\left\\vert \\begin{array}{cc}- 4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right\\vert \\\\  & = - ( 3 \\cdot  0 - 5 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) - 2 ( ( - 4 ) \\cdot  0 - 1 \\cdot  ( - 1 ) ) - ( ( - 4 ) \\cdot  5 - 1 \\cdot  3 ) \\\\  & = - 5 - 2 + 23 \\\\  & = 16.\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$, $\\overrightarrow{AC}$, and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV= \\mid 16 &= 16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534710 false] [17592186105521 1145 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$" 13194139534710 true] [17592186105832 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304788 13194139534710 true] [17592186105832 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304830 13194139534710 true] [17592186105832 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304834 13194139534710 true] [17592186105832 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304837 13194139534710 true] [17592186105832 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304840 13194139534710 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304795 13194139534710 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304802 13194139534710 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304809 13194139534710 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304843 13194139534710 true] [17592186105833 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304852 13194139534710 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304816 13194139534710 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304823 13194139534710 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304846 13194139534710 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304849 13194139534710 true] [17592186105834 1020 #edb/ref 17592186304859 13194139534710 true] [17592186304788 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304789 13194139534710 true] [17592186304788 1089 "q-128433" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304788 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534710 true] [17592186304788 1100 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨0,-1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,9,2⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,7,6⟩.$" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304788 1113 #uuid "8addc76a-7a22-5ce6-a1e9-a31f1d8601cf" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304788 1145 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}9 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+(3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 2)+4(3\\cdot 7-2\\cdot 9) \\\\  & =14+12 \\\\  & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|26|=26.\n$$" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304789 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304790 13194139534710 true] [17592186304789 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304791 13194139534710 true] [17592186304789 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304792 13194139534710 true] [17592186304789 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304793 13194139534710 true] [17592186304789 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304794 13194139534710 true] [17592186304789 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534710 true] [17592186304789 1041 "selection" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304789 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304791 13194139534710 true] [17592186304789 1110 #uuid "12fcbdbf-0e6d-5e4f-8997-9e5ade5ecd7d" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304790 1034 "38" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304790 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534710 true] [17592186304790 1111 #uuid "8fc8ae94-2946-54bd-aff9-b44c313314b0" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304791 1034 "26" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304791 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534710 true] [17592186304791 1111 #uuid "e9542f1b-d2f9-5ac0-bfe0-3203017e4fa6" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304792 1034 "66" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304792 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534710 true] [17592186304792 1111 #uuid "cc6415a9-b093-5db7-bd13-83682a0bfe5e" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304793 1034 "7" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534710 true] [17592186304793 1111 #uuid "21d53ddb-de51-560c-85bf-881912effa65" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304794 1034 "2" 13194139534710 true] [175921