}| \\\\  & =-4(3\\cdot -1-2\\cdot 2)+2(3\\cdot -1-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =28-18 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304847 1000 #edb/ref 17592186304848 13194139534710 true] [17592186304847 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534710 true] [17592186304847 1041 "field-1" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304847 1104 #edb/ref 17592186304848 13194139534710 true] [17592186304847 1110 #uuid "eeb0e33e-239e-5c78-9cc0-bd378ee4d355" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304848 1034 "10" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304848 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534710 true] [17592186304848 1111 #uuid "28e6f2fe-da70-5b2a-903b-f9ccae9614e7" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304849 1017 #edb/ref 17592186304850 13194139534710 true] [17592186304849 1089 "q-281030" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304849 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534710 true] [17592186304849 1100 "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(-1,0,1),$ $B(2,-3,4),$ $C(-2,-2,2),$ and $D(0,-1,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304849 1113 #uuid "90129f6e-2010-58a8-9c15-bbe333617408" 13194139534710 true] [17592186304849 1145 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i-3j+4k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =3i-3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-2j+2k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+1k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-j+5k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =i-j+4k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.